{% comment %}
  Local override of the al_folio_core footer.

  Two jobs:
  1. Render an empty footer, so no copyright or theme-attribution line appears.
     The element is kept so the theme's fixed-bottom layout rules still apply.
  2. Carry the site-wide accent-colour override. al-folio hard-codes
     --global-theme-color in the gem's stylesheet and exposes no config key for
     it, and the gem's <head> has no hook for extra CSS. The footer include is
     the one file on every page that this site owns, so the override lives here.

  The two values are deliberately different in lightness, not just hue. The
  theme paints publication badges with the accent and flips the badge text
  between white (light mode) and near-black (dark mode), so the light value has
  to be dark enough for white text and the dark value light enough for black
  text. Both also serve as the body link colour against their own background.
{% endcomment %}

<style>
  :root {
    --global-theme-color: #1a7f4b;
    --global-hover-color: #1a7f4b;
    /* The gem bakes the old magenta into this one as a literal rgba(), so it
       does not follow the accent above. Retint it to match. */
    --global-code-bg-color: rgba(26, 127, 75, 0.06);
  }
  html[data-theme='dark'] {
    --global-theme-color: #3fb27f;
    --global-hover-color: #3fb27f;
  }

  /* Center the icon at the theme's button size instead of the library's default. */
  #back-to-top {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }
  #back-to-top svg {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>

{% if site.footer_fixed %}
  <footer class="fixed-bottom" role="contentinfo"></footer>
{% else %}
  <footer class="sticky-bottom mt-5" role="contentinfo"></footer>
{% endif %}
